{"summary": "Ground part (items 12 and 13) is done. Every headless check passed and the browser shots are taken. Nothing is committed or published.

ITEM 13, time:
- NEW systems/time_system.gd (TimeSystem). DigSystem adds it in code as the child node "Time", so its path is the same on every peer. It holds the game clock `TimeSystem.now`, which runs 1:1 with real time.
- The server sends `_ev_clock` every 2 s and `_ev_skip` on a skip; both are rpc call_local. Each one sets DigLayer.stamp, runs DigLayer.regrow(now) and calls Chips.age(now).
- The server keeps a ledger of chip volume: every Chips.cut / wood / stones call adds to it. Chips that are 1 h old become humus: `_ev_rot` puts their exact volume into DigLayer.deposit as whole units, carrying the remainder forward. No objects remain.
- Keys​: T = +1 h, Shift+T = +1 day. The P panel has two new buttons, 'Перемотать +1 час' and '+1 день'. Any peer can ask; the server checks the amount.
- A skip also regrows picked berry bushes.
- Rates for Maxim (game time):
  - leaves blend in about 20 min, needles in about 1 h (LITTER_YEAR changed from 60 to 470 s);
  - chips rot at 1 h and leave a dark humus spot that fades over about 30 min;
  - dug earth shows its first green at 15 min, is about 36 % green after +1 h, and is all turf at 6 h (grass tufts back, it digs like turf again);
  - turf pressed flat under a log stands up again after 1 h.
- The straight strip along logs is fixed. Its cause: DigLayer.press_log marked the trough and berms as loose dug earth, which drew a brown band along every settled log. Now the berms stay turf, and the trough is marked "pressed turf" (touched = 2): no earth look, no grass, back to grass after 1 h.
- DigView meshes now carry UV.x = when the earth there moved. The shader greens it over with time, so the look ages with no mesh rebuilds.
- Grass comes back after regrowth:
  - GladeGrass.restore works from a CPU copy kept in meta, never reading the GPU buffer;
  - ValleyGrass.regrow re-scatters the chunks;
  - restored tufts are placed on the dug height, and the valley scatter uses the dug height too.

ITEM 12, ground look:
- NEW world/glade/ground_common.gdshaderinc, shared by the glade and valley ground shaders. Grass, forest floor, dug earth and litter now read as four different grounds:
  - darker greens with clumps, sparse flower drifts, softer turf detail;
  - forest floor: needle-brown carpet with clear moss cushions;
  - dug earth: dark chocolate with clay clods;
  - litter: rust needles / ochre leaves turning to black humus.
- Grass on LOW:
  - glade: a 6.5–11 m fade ring, and chunks beyond it are not drawn;
  - valley: GRASS_R on LOW changed from 0 to 13 m, with 0.6 of the density.

